@ 42.1 - Proto-Uralic to Pre-Finnic
# citation: Tropylium, from Hakulinen, Lauri (1979), “Suomen kielen rakenne ja kehitys”. Otava; Häkkinen, Kaisa (2004), “Nykysuomen etymologinen sanakirja”. WSOY; Kallio, Petri (2007), “Kantasuomen konsonanttihistoriaa”. Mémoires de la Société Finno-Ougrienne 253.
	ŋ > k / _#, in latives
	ŋ > n / _#
	{ iw, ow } > { y, u:[+long] } / _(C) (*)
	x > @ / _C
	m > n / :{ _t, _t͡sʲ, _# }:
	{ ɤ(:[+long]?), ɑ:[+long], æ:[+long] } > { ɑ(:[+long]?), o:[+long], e:[+long] } / stressed
	a > æ / {a,e,ê,i,y}(X)(C)(C)_, when unstressed
	[+affricate]w > o / unstressed (possibly analogical)
	i > e / _C, when unstressed
	iw > u / unstressed